<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Today widget provider info for API 26-30 (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5 "Widget architecture",
  "Configuration"). API 31 and later reads res/xml-v31/today_widget_info.xml instead, which adds
  maxResizeWidth/Height, targetCellWidth/Height and previewLayout, all introduced in API 31, so lint's
  UnusedAttribute check (correctly) rejects them here at minSdk 26. A `-v31` resource file replaces this
  one entirely rather than merging with it, so keep both files in step.

  Sizes match TodayGlanceWidget's SizeMode.Responsive steps in Kotlin (SMALL/MEDIUM/LARGE) so the
  launcher's default placement and the responsive breakpoints agree: 2x1 minimum (date only) up to
  3x2 (date, Gregorian line, actual weekday).

  minHeight/minResizeHeight (ROADMAP M8 T1, accessibility audit finding #15): raised from 40dp to 48dp,
  the touch-target floor docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §4 "Accessibility" sets. Unlike the Month widget's seven
  columns (finding #14), there is no shared division to account for here: the whole widget is one
  clickable region (TodayWidgetContent's outer Column carries both the tap target and its own padding),
  so its clickable height is simply the declared height itself, and 48dp both clears the floor and is
  the value used. TodayGlanceWidget.SMALL's own height moves from 40dp to 48dp to match, so the
  responsive breakpoint that shows "date only" still lines up with the true smallest resizable size.

  updatePeriodMillis is the layer-3 self-healing backstop of the midnight rollover
  (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5 "Midnight rollover (layered)"); layers 1 and 2 (the alarm and the system-event
  receivers in :core:scheduling) do the real work, so this only needs to be frequent enough to recover
  from an alarm an OEM killed, not frequent enough to matter for battery (FEATURES Q10).

  widgetCategory is "home_screen" only, deliberately not opting into "keyguard": this widget shows only
  the date, so docs/security-and-privacy.md §3.2 keeps it lock-screen eligible on Android 16 QPR2+
  (unlike a future widget that shows event titles, which declares `not_keyguard`).

  No android:configure: the optional config activity is ROADMAP M5 T4, out of scope for the Today
  widget's first version.

  previewImage (ROADMAP M5 T5) is valid since API 11 (confirmed against the SDK's own
  api-versions.xml, not from memory; CLAUDE.md rule 11's "look at the dependency's sources" applies
  equally to platform attributes), so it belongs here rather than needing its own `-v30`/`-v31` split;
  it is the widget-picker preview shown below API 31, superseded by previewLayout at API 31-34 and by
  `providePreview`/`setWidgetPreview` at API 35+ (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5 "Picker previews").
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="110dp"
    android:minHeight="48dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="110dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="48dp"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="14400000"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/today_widget_loading"
    android:previewImage="@drawable/widget_preview_image"
    android:description="@string/today_widget_description" />
